---
import { PAGE_CONTAINER } from '../utils/ui';
import Scribble from '../components/Scribble.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageTitle from '../components/PageTitle.astro';
import { CHALK, MARKS } from '../data/scribbles';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Privacy Policy | Joe Karlsson"
	description="What joekarlsson.com collects: cookieless self-hosted analytics, newsletter email addresses, and nothing loaded from Google."
	schemaType="WebPage"
>
	<div class={PAGE_CONTAINER}>
		<PageTitle title="Privacy">
			<Scribble
				{...MARKS.asterisk}
				color={CHALK}
				duration="8s"
				delay="1.2s"
				class="-top-[0.05em] -right-[0.7em] size-[0.5em]"
			/>
		</PageTitle>
		<div class="prose">
			<p>Last updated November 11, 2026</p>
			<p>
				This is a personal site that runs on a server in my house. It doesn't set cookies, and I
				don't sell or share anything about you. This page lists everything it collects and where it
				goes.
			</p>

			<h2>Analytics</h2>
			<p>
				I count visits with{' '}
				<a href="https://plausible.io/data-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
					Plausible
				</a>
				, which I run myself at plausible.joekarlsson.io, so the numbers never leave my hardware. It
				records the page you viewed, the site that sent you, your browser, operating system, device
				type and country. It also counts clicks on outbound links, file downloads and a few buttons,
				plus JavaScript errors so I can fix them. Plausible doesn't use cookies or store your IP
				address: it mixes your IP and browser into a hash with a salt that's thrown away every 24
				hours, so I can tell visits apart within a day and never across days.
			</p>

			<h2>Newsletter</h2>
			<p>
				If you subscribe, I keep your email address in listmonk, a newsletter app I run on my own
				server. Before anything else you get an email asking you to confirm. I only use the address
				to send the newsletter. Each email records whether you opened it and which links you
				clicked, so I can remove addresses that never read anything. The emails go out through{' '}
				<a
					href="https://www.brevo.com/legal/privacypolicy/"
					target="_blank"
					rel="noopener noreferrer"
				>
					Brevo
				</a>
				, a mail delivery service, which handles your address only to deliver them. Every email has
				an unsubscribe link. If you want your address deleted outright, not just unsubscribed, ask
				me and I'll delete it.
			</p>

			<h2>Hosting and Cloudflare</h2>
			<p>
				Every request goes through{' '}
				<a
					href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/"
					target="_blank"
					rel="noopener noreferrer"
				>
					Cloudflare
				</a>
				, which caches the site and blocks attacks. That means Cloudflare sees your IP address and
				the pages you request, the same as any web host would. Fonts and images all come from my own
				server: nothing on a page loads from Google.
			</p>

			<h2>Videos and embeds</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>
					<strong>YouTube.</strong> A video shows a thumbnail saved on this site. Nothing loads from
					YouTube until you press play. Then the player comes from youtube-nocookie.com, and
					Google's privacy policy applies to what you watch.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Playable projects.</strong> Some pages on /work and a couple of posts embed
					projects hosted on GitHub Pages. They only load on a desktop-sized screen, and GitHub sees
					your IP address when they do.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Amazon links.</strong> Some posts have Amazon affiliate links. If you click one,
					Amazon sets its own cookies to credit me with the sale.
				</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>Cookies and browser storage</h2>
			<p>
				This site sets no cookies. If you press the button that pauses animations, your browser
				remembers that choice in local storage. It stays on your device and never reaches me.
			</p>

			<h2>Your rights</h2>
			<p>
				You can ask what I have on you (at most, your email address), ask me to correct it, or ask
				me to delete it. That applies wherever you live, including the EU, UK and California, and
				I'll handle a request within 30 days. The legal basis for the newsletter is your consent,
				which you can take back at any time by unsubscribing.
			</p>

			<h2>Contact</h2>
			<p>
				Email questions or requests to{' '}
				<a href="mailto:newsletter@joekarlsson.com">newsletter@joekarlsson.com</a>, or reach me
				through the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>. If this policy changes, I'll update the
				date at the top.
			</p>
		</div>
	</div>
</BaseLayout>
